  "source_review": [
    "All five frozen normalizePassiveListenerOptions imports remain in the complete denominator. The already qualified owned ripple-renderer row retains its prior review. This checkpoint examines the remaining four exact import symbols, each resolving only to one top-level const initializer with literal owned options, plus every use of the normalized option constant: eighteen third-argument listener/fromEvent calls. Import escapes, type-only/private/duplicate imports, mutable aliases, writes, unknown receivers, wrong argument slots and registration/removal population drift are rejected.",
    "Authentic untouched Material16.2.14 whole legacy-slider/tooltip/tabs/menu modules supply original option initializers. Slider passive:false and the other three passive:true calls match after formatting normalization. Tabs retains its erased EventListenerOptions assertion. No golden was regenerated from candidate expectations; the original archive SHA and every retained whole module are authenticated.",
    "Complete genuine original and both advertised minimum public platform modules execute with matching actual Angular Core/compiler packages. The imported public normalizer identifies the authenticated full function body; public export/declaration chains retain AddEventListenerOptions -> AddEventListenerOptions|boolean with stable nondeprecated declarations. Complete function bodies and support-cache state agree after TypeScript AST printing removes redundant parentheses and formatting. Whole public modules are used, without extracted replacement SDK functions or product imports of private chunks.",
    "Four host-protocol profiles per genuine subject cover supported/unsupported passive option detection, SSR followed by browser detection and a throwing host feature probe followed by cached fallback. Exact owned option expressions execute, supported output retains the input object, unsupported output uses boolean capture, frozen inputs remain unchanged and feature detection stays cached. All twelve observations agree directly with the original runtime. Host window/listener objects are protocols, not a native browser-engine support qualification.",
    "Strict TypeScript6.0.3 compiles the complete genuine public platform/Core declaration closure and DOM library, skipLibCheck=false, with all four exact option calls. Six negative type controls per subject cover nonobject options, invalid passive/capture, unknown fields, boolean-output loss and missing argument. Thirteen source controls and twelve whole-module runtime mutants reject contract drift. Runtime mutants exercise identity, boolean conversion, capture fallback and cache behavior rather than replacing the SDK.",
    "No product source, HTML, CSS, SCSS, namespace binding, advertised peer/runtime floor or consumer code changes. These are public normalization dependency boundaries; complete owned component registration/removal lifecycle, native DOM/passive browser support, Angular AOT, packed/floor consumers, upstream SHA semantics, security and the complete independent audit remain separate."
